[{:adr/authoritative_for ["cloud-itonami-isco-{ISCO-08 code} 命名規則（isco- infix 必須、ISIC との衝突回避）" "kotoba-lang/occupation registry の全 436 ISCO-08 unit group 網羅と maturity tier 契約" "occupation blueprint 9 件の代表 major group 選定（0=Armed Forces は registry-only）"], :adr/supersedes [], :adr/superseded_by [], :adr/topic "cloud-itonami-isco-occupation-blueprints", :adr/related ["adr-2607011000-cloud-itonami-robotics-premise-and-isic-21-21" "adr-2606271700-cloud-itonami-business-os" "adr-2606302300-org-taxonomy-4-orgs" "adr-2607012100-cloud-itonami-org-split"], :adr/status "accepted", :adr/id "adr-2607012000-cloud-itonami-isco-occupation-blueprints", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/last_verified "2026-07-01", :adr/body "# ADR-2607012000: cloud-itonami-isco — ISCO-08 occupation blueprints (occupation counterpart to ISIC)\n\n**Status**: accepted  \n**Date**: 2026-07-01  \n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki\n\n## Decision\n\n1. New blueprint family `cloud-itonami-isco-{ISCO-08 code}`, structurally identical to `cloud-itonami-{ISIC}` (README + blueprint.edn + docs/business-model.md + docs/operator-guide.md + docs/samples/operator-console.html + AGPL-3.0-or-later + CONTRIBUTING/SECURITY/GOVERNANCE/CODE_OF_CONDUCT, robotics premise per ADR-2607011000), but keyed by occupation (1 ISCO-08 unit group = 1 sole-proprietor operator) instead of industry. The `isco-` infix is required naming — ISIC and ISCO-08 codes overlap numerically, so a bare `cloud-itonami-{code}` would be ambiguous.\n2. New registry `kotoba-lang/occupation`, mirroring `kotoba-lang/industry`'s current full-coverage state: all 436 ISCO-08 unit groups registered (sourced from `com-etzhayyim-isco`'s authoritative seed, with one upstream data-quality fix to unit 6113's corrupted name), same contract shape (`get-occupation`/`required-technologies`/`readiness`/`execution-plan`/`maturity`/`maturity-summary`/`maturity-roadmap`), same :robotics-required-on-every-entry rule.\n3. 9 curated entries (one representative unit group per non-armed-forces ISCO-08 major group) are `:maturity :blueprint` and back a published `cloud-itonami-isco-{code}` repo: 1321 Manufacturing Managers, 2221 Nursing Professionals, 3253 Community Health Workers, 4321 Stock Clerks, 5322 Home-based Personal Care Workers, 6112 Market Gardeners and Crop Growers, 7126 Plumbers and Pipe Fitters, 8332 Heavy Truck and Lorry Drivers, 9312 Civil Engineering Labourers. Major group 0 (Armed Forces Occupations) is intentionally registry-only — no sole-proprietor civilian blueprint fits it. The remaining 427 unit groups are `:spec` registry-only stubs.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- (+) Occupation classification now has a blueprint pattern symmetric with industry classification, sharing the robotics-premise contract and maturity-tier vocabulary via sibling registries.\n- (+) Full 436/436 ISCO-08 unit-group coverage, machine-readable and readiness/execution-plan/maturity-roadmap verifiable (6 tests, 47 assertions green).\n- (+) `isco-` naming infix makes the ISIC/ISCO ambiguity structurally impossible.\n- (−) Major group 0 has no blueprint repo by design.\n- (−) Known pre-existing gap, not introduced here: `kotoba-lang/industry` and `kotoba-lang/technology` predate west registration and remain unregistered in manifest/repos.edn despite ADR-2607011000 saying they should be; this ADR registers `kotoba-lang/occupation` correctly but does not retroactively fix the siblings.\n- superproject registration: `orgs/kotoba-lang/occupation` added to manifest/repos.edn / manifest/west.yml (`nbb scripts/gen-west-manifest.cljs --check` passes). The 9 blueprint repos remain standalone, per existing cloud-itonami-* convention.\n\n## Artifacts\n\n- lib (kotoba-lang org, public, Apache-2.0, pure cljc, tests green): kotoba-lang/occupation\n- blueprint repo (published under gftdcojp org, public, AGPL-3.0-or-later): cloud-itonami-isco-{1321,2221,3253,4321,5322,6112,7126,8332,9312} (9 repos)\n\n## References\n\n- ADR-2607011000 (cloud-itonami robotics premise + ISIC 21/21) — the pattern this ADR mirrors for occupations.\n- com-etzhayyim-isco (kotoba/isco-occupations.kotoba.edn) — authoritative ISCO-08 source data (619 nodes).\n- 本 ADR とペアの .md\n\n## Addendum (2026-07-01, ADR-2607012100)\n\nThe 9 cloud-itonami-isco-* blueprint repos were published under gftdcojp (public) as stated above, and have since been transferred to the dedicated cloud-itonami org per ADR-2607012100 (visibility unchanged, still public). The 'gftdcojp org' wording above is kept as the historical record of the original publish; current ownership is tracked by ADR-2607012100.", :adr/deciders ["Jun Kawasaki"], :adr/date "2026-07-01", :db/id -1, :adr/authoritative true, :adr/title "ADR-2607012000: cloud-itonami-isco — ISCO-08 occupation blueprints (occupation counterpart to ISIC)", :adr/source-format "edn"}]